cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Age of Silviculture in Uruguay
message: >-
  If you use this script or its derived products, please cite this
  repository together with the original method of Silva Junior et al.
  (2020) and the MapBiomas Uruguay Collection 3 dataset.
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-16'
authors:
  - given-names: Lucas
    family-names: Vituri Santarosa
    email: lucas.santarosa@unesp.br
    affiliation: Sao Paulo State University (UNESP)
abstract: >-
  Google Earth Engine script that maps the annual increment, extent,
  loss and age of silviculture (forest plantations) in Uruguay between
  1985 and 2024, at 30 m resolution, from the MapBiomas Uruguay
  Collection 3 land-use classification, separating Pinus (class 79)
  and Eucalyptus (class 80) plantations. Adapted from the Brazilian
  secondary-forest-age toolkit of Silva Junior et al. (2020).
keywords:
  - silviculture
  - forest plantations
  - Uruguay
  - Pinus
  - Eucalyptus
  - Pampa
  - MapBiomas Uruguay
  - Google Earth Engine
  - remote sensing
  - land use change
repository-code: https://github.com/lvsantarosa/Age-of-Silviculture-Uruguay
references:
  - type: article
    title: Benchmark maps of 33 years of secondary forest age for Brazil
    authors:
      - given-names: Celso H. L.
        family-names: Silva Junior
      - given-names: Viola H. A.
        family-names: Heinrich
      - given-names: Ana T. G.
        family-names: Freire
    journal: Scientific Data
    volume: 7
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1038/s41597-020-00600-4
